  "id": "multifunctional-antidepressant",
  "term": "multifunctional antidepressant",
  "definition": "A multifunctional antidepressant is an antidepressant-derived compound that has been altered to do more than one job, such as still interacting with monoamine transporter targets while also allowing covalent attachment and fluorescent labeling. In the source packet, this refers to a bifunctional probe designed to preserve antidepressant-like binding properties while enabling target visualization.",
